WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.734
-Welcome back, everybody.
I am here with Ryan Gosling!

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:07.667
He stars...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:09.734
They love you. They love you.
We love you.

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:13.067
He stars in that highly
anticipated new Netflix movie

00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:14.534
"The Gray Man."

00:00:14.534 --> 00:00:17.300
Now, Ryan, everyone knows that
you're an amazing movie actor,

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.300
but what a lot of people
might not know is that

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.501
you're also an
accomplished television actor.

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:25.501
And we -- Back in the '90s, we
starred in a TV show together,

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:26.701
called -- It was a crime series.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:27.701
Do you remember this?
-I remember.

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:29.033
"Tough Cop, Tough Cop."

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:31.000
-It was called
"Tough Cop, Tough Cop."

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.100
That's correct, yes.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.000
We played
two detective partners,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.667
but we were both the tough cop.

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:37.734
And, man, we didn't play
by the book at all.

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:38.801
-No. Well, I mean,
it got canceled.

00:00:38.801 --> 00:00:39.868
-It did get cancelled.

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:42.400
-It was way, way, way
too tough for TV.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:43.567
-That was the slogan.

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:44.868
The slogan was,
"It was too tough for TV."

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:47.200
-It was way too tough.
-Way too tough for TV.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.367
And it turned out to be true.

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:49.701
Anyway, you're not going to
believe this,

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:51.133
but we actually
got our hands on a clip.

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:52.868
-What?
-Yeah.

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:55.200
Here's me and Ryan Gosling
in a scene from

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.100
the '90's crime show
"Tough Cop, Tough Cop."

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.300
-Really?
-Take a look at this.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:04.634
♪♪

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:06.968
-"Tough Cop, Tough Cop."

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:11.400
-Alright, scumbag.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.634
We know you whacked
Richie Badabucco.

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:17.067
And you're going to tell us
where the body is!

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:18.667
-You don't want to talk, huh?

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:20.467
Then you're
leaving us no choice.

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:22.367
We're going to get tough.

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:25.467
-Oh, yeah,
we're going to get real tough.

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:28.501
-We're going to get so tough!

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:31.534
-We're going to -- we're going
to take you out back

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:33.834
and make you look at
how bad a job we did

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:35.901
parallel-parking my car.

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:37.934
-You got a real nice face there.

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.033
It'd be a shame if somebody

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:41.334
snapped an
unflattering photo of it.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.834
A person might
post that photo, too,

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:44.300
and maybe it becomes a meme!

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:47.234
I don't know!
-He doesn't know!

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.801
Stick out your tongue,

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:55.801
because I'm going to squirt
a dab of wasabi mustard on it.

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:57.000
Damn it, we're getting
nowhere with this guy, man.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.033
-I've never seen anything
like this.

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:00.701
It's like he's made of granite.
What do we do?

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:03.133
-I don't know what --
I know what to do.

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:06.300
-Oh.
-It's time to get medieval.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.534
You hold his arms up,
and then I'll tickle

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:11.000
the crap out of his armpits
with a feather.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.400
-You are one sick
son of a B-word.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.667
[ Laughing ] Oh! Come on!

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:17.834
-Get ready to talk,
mother[bleep]

00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:25.734
♪♪

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:29.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:31.267
-Yeah.

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:40.067
-I forgot -- I almost forgot
how intense that series was.

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:41.634
-It was really intense.

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:43.968
But, you know,
it wasn't as intense as

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:45.434
the next series
that we did, right?

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:47.601
-Oh, you mean
"Tougher Cop, Tougher Cop"?

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:49.634
-Oh, my God. You know it.

00:02:49.634 --> 00:02:52.067
-Yeah, they said that one
was too tougher for TV.

00:02:52.067 --> 00:02:53.334
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:53.334 --> 00:02:54.367
Well, you're not even
going to --

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:55.434
-It's probably
why it got canceled.

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:56.734
-It got canceled, as well.
-Yeah.

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:58.734
-It was way tougher.

00:02:58.734 --> 00:02:59.834
-It was way too tough.
-Way tougher.

00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:00.934
-You're not even going to
believe this.

00:03:00.934 --> 00:03:02.133
-What?
-I talked to the...

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:03.801
[ Laughter ]
-No.

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:05.200
-I talked to the producers.
-You have it?

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.267
-We have a clip of
that show, too, that series.

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:10.767
Here's a scene from
"Tougher Cop, Tougher Cop."

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:15.868
♪♪

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:18.367
-"Tougher Cop, Tougher Cop."

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.501
-Back again for
another round, huh?

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.367
Get up, you sick -- you sick...

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:31.534
Sit -- You sit. Sit down!

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:32.934
On the chair, normal.
Like a normal person sits.

00:03:32.934 --> 00:03:36.000
-Sit down! Sit down!
-Sit!

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.567
-Sit down! Sit down!

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:40.100
-Sit down.

00:03:42.601 --> 00:03:44.400
-Well, if you thought
we were tough before,

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:48.267
I guess you don't know the
definition of the word tough.

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:51.601
-We spent the summer
at the gym getting Jacked!

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:58.434
So you spill the beans, punk,
or I might just turn the channel

00:03:58.434 --> 00:04:01.167
when you're watching
one of your favorite shows!

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:02.868
-Alright, calm down, calm down!

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:05.667
I'm going to treat --
I'm going to treat your face

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:07.734
like the display bongo
at Guitar Center,

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:09.033
and I'm itching to play my

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:11.801
favorite Dave Matthews Band
song, "Ants Marching."

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:14.901
[ Vocalizing "Ants Marching" ]

00:04:14.901 --> 00:04:16.501
♪ He wakes up in the morning ♪

00:04:16.501 --> 00:04:18.400
Get up, get up!
Don't you disrespect me!

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:21.267
-Oh, he's got me, Jimmy!
He's got me, Jimmy!

00:04:21.267 --> 00:04:23.133
-Get off him! Get the hell off!
-Get him off me!

00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:26.300
Get him off me! Get him off me!

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.767
-Oh, you're doing
the no-hair thing now.

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:31.067
-Get him off me.
-Alright, that's it, that's it.

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:32.100
-Come on!
-What are you going to do?

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.667
What are you going to do to him?

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:35.534
-Nothing to say, huh?
That's it. I've had it.

00:04:35.534 --> 00:04:38.501
-Yeah.
-I'm done playing nice guy.

00:04:38.501 --> 00:04:40.968
Someone's going to lose
their nose!

00:04:40.968 --> 00:04:44.234
-What?!
-Yes!

00:04:44.234 --> 00:04:46.234
Who's got your nose,
you stupid mother[bleep]

00:04:46.234 --> 00:04:48.968
-Stupid mother[bleep]

00:04:48.968 --> 00:04:56.067
♪♪

00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:58.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:09.133 --> 00:05:12.601
-They don't make --
they don't make TV like that.

00:05:12.601 --> 00:05:13.801
You wear your jacket
the same as me.

00:05:13.801 --> 00:05:16.467
-Yeah, you know,
just my style, man.

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:18.767
-Yeah. They don't make TV
like that anymore,

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:20.033
I got to say.

00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:21.133
-You know, I guess --
But I guess

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:22.267
that's why it got cancelled.

00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:23.434
People couldn't handle it.
-That's true.

00:05:23.434 --> 00:05:24.968
But we did have
one last spin-off, though.

00:05:24.968 --> 00:05:26.801
-Yeah, that's true.
"Toughest Cop, Toughest Cop."

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:29.067
-"Toughest Cop, Toughest Cop."

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:30.234
And we actually have
a scene from the show.

00:05:30.234 --> 00:05:32.367
-And it was way too toughest.
-We have a clip.

00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:33.434
-Way too toughest.

00:05:33.434 --> 00:05:34.801
-You're not even
going to believe this.

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.400
-How are we getting these?
-We have a clip. Here we go.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.767
-This is a
blast from the past, man.

00:05:38.767 --> 00:05:43.801
♪♪

00:05:43.801 --> 00:05:46.801
-"Toughest Cop, Toughest Cop."

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:50.167
-Oh!

00:05:50.167 --> 00:05:51.400
Oh!

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:55.634
Surprise, surprise.
Look who's back.

00:05:55.634 --> 00:05:57.200
Huh?

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:59.234
After three years,
you're finally going to talk?

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:00.467
Huh?

00:06:01.567 --> 00:06:03.634
One slap is all it takes.

00:06:03.634 --> 00:06:06.300
-Sit down! Sit down!

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.300
-Your hair?
You want to put your hair on?

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.434
You want to put your hair on?
-Put your hair on!

00:06:10.434 --> 00:06:14.601
-Yeah.
Your mustache is on his head.

00:06:14.601 --> 00:06:17.901
That doesn't belong there,
and you know that!

00:06:17.901 --> 00:06:18.968
That's his mustache!

00:06:18.968 --> 00:06:20.801
-That's mine!
-That's his mustache!

00:06:20.801 --> 00:06:22.100
-Give me that!
-Give me that beard.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:24.834
And he wears your beard, okay?
That's the way it works.

00:06:24.834 --> 00:06:26.467
You want to be tough now?
-Who's got your beard?!

00:06:26.467 --> 00:06:28.400
-Who's got your beard, dude?
-You're gonna take my mustache?

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:30.467
-Who's got your beard, dude?

00:06:30.467 --> 00:06:32.734
Now, listen to me.

00:06:32.734 --> 00:06:36.033
I'm gonna tell you something.
-Sit down!

00:06:36.033 --> 00:06:38.067
-Now, listen, you know what
I'm going to do?

00:06:38.067 --> 00:06:39.067
-Talk to him.
Talk to him, Jimmy.

00:06:39.067 --> 00:06:41.200
-Give me this.
-I got him.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:44.467
I got him.
-Don't kick me.

00:06:44.467 --> 00:06:45.868
Now, listen.

00:06:48.467 --> 00:06:50.968
We can do this.

00:06:50.968 --> 00:06:53.100
-Just throw him up.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.868
-Alright, now listen.
You want to talk?

00:06:55.868 --> 00:06:57.801
You gonna talk now, dude?
You going to talk?

00:06:57.801 --> 00:06:59.400
-Oh!
-Oh, geez.

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:01.234
-Oh!
-You going to talk?

00:07:01.234 --> 00:07:02.834
-Sit down.
-Now, listen to me.

00:07:02.834 --> 00:07:04.968
You start talking right now.
What are you going to do to him?

00:07:04.968 --> 00:07:06.133
Tell him what
you're going to do to him.

00:07:06.133 --> 00:07:08.300
-If you don't
start talking right now --

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:09.634
-Pull your shirt down,
you sick --

00:07:09.634 --> 00:07:11.334
-Pull it down!

00:07:12.868 --> 00:07:14.868
If you don't start
talking right now,

00:07:14.868 --> 00:07:17.634
I'm going to whisper
into my partner's ear,

00:07:17.634 --> 00:07:21.067
and he's going to laugh so hard.

00:07:21.067 --> 00:07:24.234
And for the rest of your
worthless life,

00:07:24.234 --> 00:07:27.400
you're going to wonder
what that joke was!

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.267
-Yeah, that's right! Now, look.

00:07:29.267 --> 00:07:32.801
Take my mustache,
and you wear my mustache.

00:07:32.801 --> 00:07:34.567
-Yeah.
-And guess what.

00:07:34.567 --> 00:07:36.868
Get ready to be
pile-drived, dude.

00:07:36.868 --> 00:07:39.234
You sick mother[bleep]

00:07:39.234 --> 00:07:43.434
♪♪

00:07:43.434 --> 00:07:46.934
-It still holds up.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:46.934 --> 00:07:48.801
My thanks to Ryan Gosling.

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:50.267
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:07:50.267 --> 00:07:51.634
Stick around, everybody.
Come on back.

